WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.078
Let's summarize the major ideas from Module 6 Start
with grain

00:00:06.988 --> 00:00:12.618
Decide what one result row should represent before
writing a join Then

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:18.371
choose preservation INNER JOIN keeps only matches
LEFT and RIGHT

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:23.832
preserve one designated side FULL OUTER JOIN
preserves unmatched rows from both

00:00:23.858 --> 00:00:29.589
sources Remember that ON controls matching while
WHERE filters the joined

00:00:29.602 --> 00:00:36.845
result This distinction is especially important with
outer joins Cardinality

00:00:36.871 --> 00:00:42.545
explains why rows repeat or multiply One-to-many
repetition can be completely

00:00:42.571 --> 00:00:47.387
correct but several one-to-many child tables joined
together can create combinations that

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.351
inflate counts When your target is one row per
patient or one

00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:59.090
row per department pre-aggregating child tables is
often the clearest solution Finally

00:00:59.288 --> 00:01:05.264
validate Compare row counts distinct keys unmatched
cases and known examples

00:01:06.994 --> 00:01:09.954
If you keep one habit from this module let it be
this

00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:14.007
define the grain predict the matches run the join
and verify the

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.415
result before trusting it
